### ConfigurationFactory merging/defaulting logic

Source: https://github.com/infection/infection/blob/master/src/Configuration/ConfigurationFactory.php

How the 5 config keys are merged from CLI options and schema defaults in the ConfigurationFactory. Key details: testFramework defaults to 'phpunit', threads defaults to max(1, cpuCores-1), minMsi/maxTimeouts use ?? fallback from CLI to schema.

```php
$testFramework ??= $schema->testFramework ?? TestFrameworkTypes::PHPUNIT;
// ...
minMsi: self::retrieveMinMsi($minMsi, $schema),
// ...
threadCount: $this->retrieveThreadCount($threadCount, $schema),
// ...
phpUnit: $this->retrievePhpUnit($schema, $configDir),
// ...
source: $schema->source,
```

--------------------------------

### PHPUnit declares --testsuite as initial-run-only

Source: https://github.com/infection/infection/blob/master/src/TestFramework/PhpUnit/Adapter/PhpUnitAdapter.php

The PHPUnit adapter explicitly lists --testsuite as an option that should only be passed to the initial run, not to mutant runs.

```php
public function getInitialRunOnlyOptions(): array
{
    return ['--configuration', '--filter', '--testsuite'];
}
```

--------------------------------

### Scalar config options: timeout, threads, minMsi

Source: https://github.com/infection/infection/blob/master/resources/schema.json

Defines the timeout (seconds, number >=0), threads (positive int or 'max'), and minMsi (0-100 percentage) configuration keys from the JSON schema

```json
"timeout": {
    "type": "number",
    "description": "The allowed timeout in seconds.",
    "minimum": "0"
},
"threads": {
    "oneOf": [
        {
            "type": "integer",
            "minimum": 1
        },
        {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": ["max"]
        }
    ]
},
"minMsi": {
    "type": "number",
    "minimum": 0,
    "maximum": 100,
    "description": "Minimum Mutation Score Indicator (MSI) percentage value. Should be used in CI server."
}
```

--------------------------------

### Mutant test run filters out initial-run-only options like --testsuite

Source: https://github.com/infection/infection/blob/master/src/TestFramework/LegacyTestFrameworkBridge.php

test() passes filtered options via getFilteredExtraOptionsForMutant(), which strips options declared as initial-run-only by the adapter.

```php
public function test(Mutant $mutant): MutantProcessContainer
{
    return $this->processFactory->create(
        $this->adapter,
        $mutant,
        $this->getFilteredExtraOptionsForMutant(),
    );
}

private function getFilteredExtraOptionsForMutant(): string
{
    if ($this->adapter instanceof ProvidesInitialRunOnlyOptions) {
        return $this->testFrameworkExtraOptionsFilter->filterForMutantProcess(
            $this->config->testFrameworkExtraOptions,
            $this->adapter->getInitialRunOnlyOptions(),
        );
    }

    return $this->config->testFrameworkExtraOptions;
}
```

